### What this does

| Request type | What the middleware sends back |
|--------------|--------------------------------|
| **Simple CORS request** (e.g. `GET /api/hello` from an allowed origin) | `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: <origin>`<br>`Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true`<br>`Vary: Origin` |
| **Pre‑flight** (`OPTIONS /api/hello`) | Same headers **plus** `Access-Control-Allow-Methods` & `Access-Control-Allow-Headers` (and optional `Access-Control-Max-Age`). Responds with **204 No Content** and ends the request. |
| **Disallowed origin** | `403 Origin not allowed` (you can change this to just `next()` if you prefer silent failure). |

